### 2. Node.js backend — replace mock DKT with real HTTP call

#### [MODIFY] [ai.service.js](file:///d:/GamifiedLearning/backend/src/services/ai.service.js)

Replace the mock `getDKTPrediction` with a real HTTP call to `http://localhost:8000/quiz/submit`.

The function will:
1. Accept `(userId, topicSlug, concept, difficulty, correct)` — not just `priorMastery`.
2. POST to the ml-backend with these fields.
3. Parse the response: `{ mastery, next_level, concept_complete, xp_earned, full_mastery }`.
4. Return a normalized result matching what `quiz.controller.js` expects:
   - `updated`: the concept's per-difficulty mastery scores
   - `nextDifficulty`: `next_level`
   - `readyToAdvanceConcept`: `concept_complete`

#### [MODIFY] [quiz.controller.js](file:///d:/GamifiedLearning/backend/src/controllers/quiz.controller.js)

Update the `submitQuiz` handler to pass the new parameters to `getDKTPrediction`:
- Pass `userId`, `topicSlug` (normalized from `topic.title`), `concept`, `difficulty`, `passed ? 1 : 0`

#### [NEW] `backend/src/utils/topicSlug.js`

A small utility to convert a Topic title (e.g. `"Python Fundamentals"`) into the DKT slug format (e.g. `"python_fundamentals"`), matching the keys in `ml-backend/app/dkt/skills.py`.

#### [MODIFY] `backend/.env`

Add `ML_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000`

