## Key Design Decisions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Single source of truth for mastery**: The Node.js backend remains the master store of mastery (MongoDB `Mastery` collection). The ml-backend is stateless for the inference result — it saves interaction history and returns scores, but the Node.js backend writes the final authoritative `Mastery` document.

> [!NOTE]
> **Topic slug normalization**: The Node.js backend stores topic titles as human-readable strings (e.g. "Python Fundamentals"). The DKT model uses snake_case slugs (e.g. "python_fundamentals"). A utility function handles this mapping.

> [!NOTE]
> **Graceful fallback**: If the ml-backend is unreachable (e.g. not running), the Node.js backend falls back to the existing mock arithmetic to avoid breaking the quiz flow. A warning is logged.

